# .kb-aliases.env: aliases for confidential terms. LOCAL ONLY: git-ignored, never committed or published.
#
# Write ALIAS=real term, one per line. Separate other spellings of the same term with |.
# Everywhere in the KB, in commits, code repos and forge posts, write only the ALIAS.
# The agent reads this file to know what each alias means, and `kb.py check`, `kb.py ops post`
# and `kb.py leak-check` fail if a real term slips out (shown masked as [ALIAS]).
#
# Share this file with trusted collaborators by hand (password manager, encrypted chat).
# There is no committed copy on purpose. Teammates ask the owner for it.
#
# Examples (delete them):
# FB=foobar|Foo Bar Inc
# CLIENT_A=Globex Corporation
# CODENAME=Project Nightjar
